{"content_hash": "1a8c0a3c704e42c0", "version_id": 704, "article_id": 71, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "Japan launches mission to bring back a piece of Mars's moon", "title_zh": "日本发射探测器，要把火星卫星的碎片带回地球", "has_translation": true, "topic": "science", "source": "bbc_science", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmvgxvkv54w1o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1697689806591-e5e4269f10eb?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8OXx8bWlzc2lvbiUyMHNldCUyMGJsYXN0fGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTIzNjYxMjd8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Behnam Mohsenzadeh on Unsplash", "author": "Behnam Mohsenzadeh", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@bmohsenzadeh?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-bunch-of-smoke-is-billowing-out-of-a-building-Q5vwV1Xyor4?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(235, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(273, 46%, 48%)", "label": "SCIENCE", "seed": "b923fc532535"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-19", "word_count": 232, "reading_minutes": 1.2, "lead": "A Japanese spacecraft is set to launch on Monday and will try to collect dust from Phobos, one of Mars's two moons. If it succeeds, it will be the first sample ever brought back from Mars or its moons.", "lead_zh": "日本的一艘探测器将于周一发射，尝试从火星的两颗卫星之一——火卫一上采集尘埃。如果成功，这将是人类首次从火星或其卫星带回样本。", "preview": "The Mars Moons Exploration (MMX) mission is led by the Japanese Space Agency and will blast off from Japan. The spacecraft is expected to ar", "preview_zh": "火星卫星探测计划（MMX）由日本宇宙航空研究开发机构牵头，将从日本发射升空。探测器预计于2027年8月抵达火卫一。火卫一非常小，直径只有约20公里，形状有点像一颗太空土豆。太阳系内圈只有三颗卫星：我们的月球、火卫一和火卫二。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 695, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/71/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 82.45, "size_bytes": 495648, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 260, "has_timeline": true, "alternates": [{"voice": "af_bella", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/71/en_b2_af_bella.mp3", "duration": 84.0, "size_bytes": 505008, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 260, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/71/en_b2_af_bella.json"}, {"voice": "am_michael", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/71/en_b2_am_michael.mp3", "duration": 89.25, "size_bytes": 536400, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 260, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/71/en_b2_am_michael.json"}, {"voice": "bf_emma", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/71/en_b2_bf_emma.mp3", "duration": 77.025, "size_bytes": 463104, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 260, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/71/en_b2_bf_emma.json"}, {"voice": "bm_george", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/71/en_b2_bm_george.mp3", "duration": 82.5, "size_bytes": 495936, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 260, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/71/en_b2_bm_george.json"}]}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@dcbf67c/content/data/versions/704.json", "paragraphs": ["The Mars Moons Exploration (MMX) mission is led by the Japanese Space Agency and will blast off from Japan. The spacecraft is expected to arrive at Phobos in August 2027. Phobos is tiny, only about 20km across, and it is shaped a little like a space potato. There are just three moons in the inner Solar System: our Moon, Phobos and Deimos.", "Landing on such a small moon is difficult. Phobos has very little gravity of its own, but it sits next to Mars, whose gravity is much stronger. A small rover will be sent down first to find a safe landing site. The main spacecraft will then touch down and use a robotic arm to pick up about 10g of moon dust.", "That sample will be packed into a small capsule and returned to Earth in 2031, landing in the desert of South Australia. Scientists believe the dust will help explain where Mars's moons came from. One idea is that a space rock hit Mars long ago and the debris formed the moons. The other is that the moons are asteroids captured by Mars's gravity.", "The sample may also contain grains of Mars itself, because impacts on the planet can throw material onto Phobos. Nasa's Perseverance rover has been collecting Martian samples, but its return mission was cancelled after US funding stopped. China plans its own Mars sampling mission in 2028."], "paragraphs_zh": ["火星卫星探测计划（MMX）由日本宇宙航空研究开发机构牵头，将从日本发射升空。探测器预计于2027年8月抵达火卫一。火卫一非常小，直径只有约20公里，形状有点像一颗太空土豆。太阳系内圈只有三颗卫星：我们的月球、火卫一和火卫二。", "在这么小的卫星上着陆并不容易。火卫一自身引力很弱，但它紧邻火星，而火星的引力要强得多。科研团队会先放下一辆小型巡视器，寻找安全的着陆点。随后主探测器着陆，用机械臂采集约10克月球尘埃。", "这些样本将被装入一个小胶囊，于2031年返回地球，降落在南澳大利亚的沙漠中。科学家相信，这些尘埃有助于解释火星卫星的起源。一种观点认为，很久以前一颗太空岩石撞上火星，碎片形成了这两颗卫星；另一种观点认为，它们是火星引力捕获的小行星。", "样本中可能还含有火星本身的颗粒，因为火星表面的撞击会把物质抛到火卫一上。美国宇航局的“毅力号”巡视器一直在收集火星样本，但其取样返回任务因美国停止拨款而取消。中国计划在2028年开展自己的火星采样任务。"], "body": "The Mars Moons Exploration (MMX) mission is led by the Japanese Space Agency and will blast off from Japan. The spacecraft is expected to arrive at Phobos in August 2027. Phobos is tiny, only about 20km across, and it is shaped a little like a space potato. There are just three moons in the inner Solar System: our Moon, Phobos and Deimos.\n\nLanding on such a small moon is difficult. Phobos has very little gravity of its own, but it sits next to Mars, whose gravity is much stronger. A small rover will be sent down first to find a safe landing site. The main spacecraft will then touch down and use a robotic arm to pick up about 10g of moon dust.\n\nThat sample will be packed into a small capsule and returned to Earth in 2031, landing in the desert of South Australia. Scientists believe the dust will help explain where Mars's moons came from. One idea is that a space rock hit Mars long ago and the debris formed the moons. The other is that the moons are asteroids captured by Mars's gravity.\n\nThe sample may also contain grains of Mars itself, because impacts on the planet can throw material onto Phobos. Nasa's Perseverance rover has been collecting Martian samples, but its return mission was cancelled after US funding stopped. China plans its own Mars sampling mission in 2028.", "body_zh": "火星卫星探测计划（MMX）由日本宇宙航空研究开发机构牵头，将从日本发射升空。探测器预计于2027年8月抵达火卫一。火卫一非常小，直径只有约20公里，形状有点像一颗太空土豆。太阳系内圈只有三颗卫星：我们的月球、火卫一和火卫二。\n\n在这么小的卫星上着陆并不容易。火卫一自身引力很弱，但它紧邻火星，而火星的引力要强得多。科研团队会先放下一辆小型巡视器，寻找安全的着陆点。随后主探测器着陆，用机械臂采集约10克月球尘埃。\n\n这些样本将被装入一个小胶囊，于2031年返回地球，降落在南澳大利亚的沙漠中。科学家相信，这些尘埃有助于解释火星卫星的起源。一种观点认为，很久以前一颗太空岩石撞上火星，碎片形成了这两颗卫星；另一种观点认为，它们是火星引力捕获的小行星。\n\n样本中可能还含有火星本身的颗粒，因为火星表面的撞击会把物质抛到火卫一上。美国宇航局的“毅力号”巡视器一直在收集火星样本，但其取样返回任务因美国停止拨款而取消。中国计划在2028年开展自己的火星采样任务。", "text": "The Mars Moons Exploration (MMX) mission is led by the Japanese Space Agency and will blast off from Japan. The spacecraft is expected to arrive at Phobos in August 2027. Phobos is tiny, only about 20km across, and it is shaped a little like a space potato. There are just three moons in the inner Solar System: our Moon, Phobos and Deimos. Landing on such a small moon is difficult. Phobos has very little gravity of its own, but it sits next to Mars, whose gravity is much stronger. A small rover will be sent down first to find a safe landing site. The main spacecraft will then touch down and use a robotic arm to pick up about 10g of moon dust. That sample will be packed into a small capsule and returned to Earth in 2031, landing in the desert of South Australia. Scientists believe the dust will help explain where Mars's moons came from. One idea is that a space rock hit Mars long ago and the debris formed the moons. The other is that the moons are asteroids captured by Mars's gravity. The sample may also contain grains of Mars itself, because impacts on the planet can throw material onto Phobos. Nasa's Perseverance rover has been collecting Martian samples, but its return mission was cancelled after US funding stopped. China plans its own Mars sampling mission in 2028.", "vocab": [{"word": "blast off", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "发射升空", "note": "常用于火箭、飞船发射", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "sample", "pos": "noun", "zh": "样本", "note": "科学语境中常指采集回来的物质", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "mission", "pos": "noun", "zh": "任务；探测计划", "note": "space mission 指太空探测任务", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "gravity", "pos": "noun", "zh": "引力；重力", "note": "不可数名词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "rover", "pos": "noun", "zh": "巡视器；探测车", "note": "在星球表面移动探测的装置", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "terrain", "pos": "noun", "zh": "地形；地势", "note": "常指某片区域的地面状况", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "capsule", "pos": "noun", "zh": "太空舱；胶囊", "note": "这里指返回舱", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "debris", "pos": "noun", "zh": "碎片；残骸", "note": "不可数名词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "asteroid", "pos": "noun", "zh": "小行星", "note": "太阳系中的岩石天体", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "capture", "pos": "verb", "zh": "捕获；俘获", "note": "这里指引力把天体“抓住”", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "composition", "pos": "noun", "zh": "成分；构成", "note": "化学、矿物语境常用", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "pristine", "pos": "adj", "zh": "原始的；未受污染的", "note": "强调样本保持原样", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "fetched_at": "2026-10-18T23:28:46.282887", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "The", "s": 0.275, "e": 0.375, "sm": 275, "em": 374, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Mars", "s": 0.375, "e": 0.787, "sm": 375, "em": 787, "cs": 4, "ce": 8, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "Moons", "s": 0.787, "e": 1.125, "sm": 787, "em": 1125, "cs": 9, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "Exploration", "s": 1.125, "e": 2.163, "sm": 1125, "em": 2162, "cs": 15, "ce": 26, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "(", "s": 2.163